WEBVTT

1
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.030
(ALL SHOUTING)

2
00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:58.156
Come on, McLean! You fucking mug!

3
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.597
- Come on!
- I ain't done yet.

4
00:01:13.319 --> 00:01:14.355
(GROANS)

5
00:01:22.719 --> 00:01:24.518
(SINGING) <i># Crazy</i>

6
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.631
<i># Crazy for feeling so lonely.</i>

7
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.680
Come on, boy. Right here. Right here.

8
00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:42.192
(SINGING) <i># Worry</i>

9
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.671
<i># Why do I let myself worry? #</i>

10
00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:54.756
(GROANS)

11
00:02:34.039 --> 00:02:35.712
(GROANING)

12
00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:58.716
(GROANING)

13
00:04:29.519 --> 00:04:30.589
What've you done?

14
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:33.875
I've wet meself.

15
00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:36.072
You filthy bastard!

16
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.194
My dad is coming back soon.

17
00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:41.316
No, boy!

18
00:04:43.519 --> 00:04:45.398
I'm the guv'nor here. Your dad is dead!

19
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.956
I'm your stepdad now, that's the end of it!

20
00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:51.715
JIM: <i>Your dad is dead, shut your crying!</i>

21
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:52.836
LITTLE LENNY: <i>Mum's the guv'nor.</i>

22
00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.399
I'm the guv'nor.

23
00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.235
(JIM SINGING) <i># A lady grabbed my arm</i>

24
00:04:57.319 --> 00:05:00.596
<i># She said, "You look a man on the pluck!"</i>

25
00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:03.992
<i># It might cost a tenner,</i>
<i>it might cost a bob! #</i>

26
00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:10.076
It depends on the size of your mug!

27
00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.790
LENNY: <i>Nine, ten. Nine, ten.</i>

28
00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:15.910
<i>Nine, ten.</i>

29
00:05:18.839 --> 00:05:19.875
LENNY: Tea, Val?

30
00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.393
Oh, lovely.

31
00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.120
Len, slow down.

32
00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.512
Oh, mmm.

33
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.076
Give me your hands.

34
00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.870
No, no, no, no.

35
00:05:51.399 --> 00:05:52.629
I'm alright.

36
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.639
We're late for the rent again, Len.

37
00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.757
You said that we wouldn't have
to go into the pot.

38
00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.353
Leave it with me, Val.

39
00:06:03.399 --> 00:06:04.720
(DOGS BARKING OUTSIDE)

40
00:06:06.759 --> 00:06:09.115
VAL: Lenny, I've made your breakfast.

41
00:06:09.959 --> 00:06:11.110
I'm off, Val.

42
00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.879
Lenny, what time are you going to be home?

43
00:06:15.839 --> 00:06:17.274
Carrots!

44
00:06:33.079 --> 00:06:34.274
Carrots.

45
00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.033
- Lenny.
- Hello, my son.

46
00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.634
How are you feeling today, boy?

47
00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.029
Strong as you like, Carrots,
strong as you like.

48
00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.156
Hey, when are you going to
get a proper job, boy, hey?

49
00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.593
Done with all that street rugging.

50
00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.913
Oh, you will get your collar felt,
you will, with all that soppy graft.

51
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.798
Well, listen, the world is changing, boy.

52
00:06:49.879 --> 00:06:51.360
It's not like when we was nippers.

53
00:06:51.439 --> 00:06:54.319
You know, you got to have
an angle or a bit of cutlery

54
00:06:54.399 --> 00:06:56.197
and you have got to get into something, boy.

55
00:06:56.439 --> 00:06:59.159
I promise you, boy,
what I do is not technically illegal.

56
00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.800
Oh, technically illegal?
You are an armed robber.

57
00:07:01.879 --> 00:07:05.634
No. I am more like a... More like a saint.

58
00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.394
Redistributing wealth. It's quite spiritual.

59
00:07:08.519 --> 00:07:09.636
- (SIGHS)
- Karma, boy.

60
00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:10.755
That'll get steam on the table.

61
00:07:10.839 --> 00:07:11.910
Here you go, Teresa.

62
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.798
You need a couple of
new wheels on there, babe.

63
00:07:13.879 --> 00:07:15.108
Alright boys, how are you?

64
00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:17.795
Come on, come on.
Put 'em up, put 'em up. Right here.

65
00:07:17.879 --> 00:07:20.713
Oh, harder. Oh, harder. Oh!

66
00:07:21.199 --> 00:07:22.428
Hello, hello mate.

67
00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.031
Come on, boy. Have a look at your boat, then.

68
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.759
Look like Godzilla, boy.

69
00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.274
I've got character.

70
00:07:29.879 --> 00:07:31.711
Hands like broken melons.

71
00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.276
Proper use, boy. Potentialise yourself.

72
00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.115
Alright, good soul, good boy.

73
00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:38.838
Yeah, you have got to potentialise yourself.

74
00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.036
Put them to proper use.

75
00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.269
What do you mean, "Proper use"?

76
00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.000
I have three gypsy fights
lined up off my cousin Bootnose.

77
00:07:44.079 --> 00:07:47.072
No, listen. I mean, in the ring, boy.

78
00:07:47.439 --> 00:07:48.759
The ring?

79
00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:53.759
Carrots, I love you. You are my cousin,
but gloves are for poofs, alright?

80
00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.240
- Come on.
- Alright.

81
00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.033
Here, Trevor.

82
00:07:57.319 --> 00:07:58.355
Hiya, Lenny.

83
00:07:58.439 --> 00:08:01.238
I heard you been selling
that shit around my manor again.

84
00:08:01.319 --> 00:08:02.355
That gospel?

85
00:08:02.439 --> 00:08:03.839
Look, someone's been telling
you rubbish, boy.

86
00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.833
Well, if I find out it's true,
I'm coming after you

87
00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:07.956
and I'm gonna hurt you.

88
00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.360
- Hurt you!
- OK. OK, Lenny.

89
00:08:09.439 --> 00:08:11.237
And then I'm gonna feed it to you.

90
00:08:11.759 --> 00:08:13.432
- OK, Lenny.
- Fuck off!

91
00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.435
Hello, Katie. Come here, sweetheart.

92
00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.709
- Are you alright?
- Yeah.

93
00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.792
- You look beautiful, my love.
- Thank you.

94
00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:22.314
Go on, have a good one.

95
00:08:22.399 --> 00:08:23.959
- Hello, Frank.
- Right.

96
00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.158
- Lenny.
- LENNY: Alright.

97
00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:29.512
Oh, have a look at her, Len.
She's golden, isn't she?

98
00:08:29.959 --> 00:08:31.189
She's hovering.

99
00:08:31.399 --> 00:08:33.312
God. She could straighten up Liberace.

100
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.158
Hello, Treacle, this is Trixie.

101
00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:38.198
This is Sue's girl, Carrots.
Trixie, this is Carrots.

102
00:08:38.279 --> 00:08:39.759
Don't mind him, he is a little bit

103
00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.558
highly strung at present,
he's just got out of prison.

104
00:08:41.639 --> 00:08:42.960
- Oi.
- (LAUGHS)

105
00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:44.832
You are actually just the man
I've been looking for.

106
00:08:44.919 --> 00:08:45.956
Oh, yeah?

107
00:08:46.039 --> 00:08:47.678
How do you fancy doing
a little favour for me?

108
00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.432
That Alan's been giving me mum agg again.

109
00:08:50.559 --> 00:08:52.630
Seems he won't take no for an answer.

110
00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.836
Keeps banging on the
door come 3:00 in the morning.

111
00:08:54.919 --> 00:08:57.071
I can see he's got you all aeriated.

112
00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.235
You leave it with me, alright?
I'll sort it out.

113
00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.918
Thanks, Len, that will mean the world to us.

114
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.035
Good girl.

115
00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.397
I would drink your bathwater, I would.

116
00:09:08.919 --> 00:09:10.433
Full of yourself, ain't ya?

117
00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.068
I'll empty out later.

118
00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.355
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

119
00:09:13.799 --> 00:09:15.028
- Alright.
- Ta-ta.

120
00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.155
Ta-ra.

121
00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.316
(SINGING) <i># As I was walking past St Paul's</i>

122
00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.114
<i># A lady grabbed me by the arm</i>

123
00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.000
<i># She said, "You look a man on pluck!" #</i>

124
00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.917
Oh, morning, Alan.

125
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.195
CARROTS: Speak of the devil.

126
00:09:32.279 --> 00:09:35.956
So, what is this I hear about
you terrorising Sue

127
00:09:36.039 --> 00:09:38.395
and her little girl Trixie, hmm?

128
00:09:38.519 --> 00:09:41.159
No, Len, I ain't, I swear.

129
00:09:41.799 --> 00:09:45.679
You swear. Well, someone's
telling porkies, Alan.

130
00:09:45.919 --> 00:09:48.037
Is it you or is it her?

131
00:09:49.279 --> 00:09:50.429
I'll drop round.

132
00:09:50.559 --> 00:09:52.677
I mean, it's only when
I've had a drink I swing round there.

133
00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.559
Oh, it's only when you've had a drink?

134
00:09:55.279 --> 00:09:57.794
Well, you're having a drink
right now, aren't you, Alan?

135
00:09:57.879 --> 00:09:59.109
Does that mean you are going
over there again?

136
00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.235
Giving her agg?

137
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.953
Have I got to hurt you, Alan?

138
00:10:02.159 --> 00:10:03.275
Have I got to hurt him, Carrots?

139
00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.999
I am going to fucking hurt you, Alan?

140
00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:06.235
Leave off.

141
00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.351
I've just been paid,
I just fancied I'd have a lager.

142
00:10:08.679 --> 00:10:09.716
Oh, that's it then.

143
00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:14.272
Funny thing, Al,
you owe me a couple, didn't ya?

144
00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.273
- There you go.
- Thank fuck you bumped into me, Al.

145
00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.913
Now, you are going to go round Sue's

146
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.152
and you are going to give this to her
and you are going to apologise.

147
00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:26.955
You are going to say you ain't
never going to bother her again.

148
00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.591
And then you are going to come back here
and you are going to tell me what she said.

149
00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:35.955
Fuck off, then.

150
00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:41.149
Go on, Alan, I ain't got all fucking day!

151
00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.436
- (BOTH LAUGH)
- What a mug.

152
00:10:46.399 --> 00:10:48.596
- Hello, ladies.
- Hello, Carol.

153
00:10:49.519 --> 00:10:51.398
Oh, it's a lovely sight, look at that.

154
00:10:51.519 --> 00:10:52.840
You've nicked one of these before.

155
00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.440
- Morning, Len.
- Morning.

156
00:10:54.559 --> 00:10:55.960
We've a couple of them, haven't we?

157
00:10:56.519 --> 00:10:59.159
The Rozzers ain't catching you in that,
I tell you that, boy.

158
00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.235
Chaps.

159
00:11:01.799 --> 00:11:02.916
Fellas.

160
00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:10.071
- Carrots, how are you doing, son?
- Hey!

161
00:11:10.159 --> 00:11:12.549
- Alright, how is Lenny?
- Top of the world.

162
00:11:12.799 --> 00:11:14.677
MAN: Good boy. Stay out of trouble.

163
00:11:15.399 --> 00:11:16.720
- WOMAN: Carrots?
- Leslie!

164
00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.360
- Len, boy.
- LENNY: Hello.

165
00:11:18.639 --> 00:11:19.789
- CARROTS: Les!
- Carrots!

166
00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:21.109
LENNY: How's Douglas Haig, then, eh?

167
00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.600
Are you still farting mackerel?

168
00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.756
You two still on speaking terms?

169
00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.636
Already been half poisoned.

170
00:11:27.919 --> 00:11:29.751
Empty as a whore's handbag.

171
00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:32.071
- Who poisoned him?
- LESLIE: Reenie.

172
00:11:32.639 --> 00:11:35.677
Left a bucket of Gordon's
out on the side again.

173
00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.431
Silly moo. Doggy drunk himself half to death.

174
00:11:40.159 --> 00:11:44.120
They found him in a skip,
Wednesday week and he's... (CHUCKLING)

175
00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.759
Alright now. He's great.

176
00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.592
Look at the smile on him.

177
00:11:49.519 --> 00:11:51.557
LENNY: He ain't smiling, old timer.

178
00:11:51.679 --> 00:11:53.000
Look at him, his lip sticks out.

179
00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:56.356
Better top up his sherry, then, boy.
Always calms him down.

180
00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.793
Get me a pint while you're there.

181
00:11:59.159 --> 00:12:01.116
You ain't bought a drink since
the Blitz, have you?

182
00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.918
I ain't had any rump since then, neither.

183
00:12:03.639 --> 00:12:05.552
Shrapnel blew me bollocks off.

184
00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.519
Here, show Lenny your letter from the Queen.

185
00:12:07.759 --> 00:12:10.600
LENNY:
Say, Carrots, he was in the Somme, Leslie.

186
00:12:10.759 --> 00:12:11.875
CARROTS: I know.

187
00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.548
And you came back with what,
half a plastic leg,

188
00:12:14.639 --> 00:12:17.519
four bouts of syphilis
and someone else's dignity, didn't you?

189
00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.398
Yeah, and I would do it all
again if I had half a chance.

190
00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.758
(BOBBY SINGING)

191
00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.068
- Beautiful, Bobby.
<i>- Oh, thank you very much, gentlemen.</i>

192
00:12:27.159 --> 00:12:29.072
<i>Thank you, Leslie. Thank you, Carrots.</i>

193
00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.111
He's a sociable man.

194
00:12:32.039 --> 00:12:35.158
Never leave your children unattended
with him, mind you.

195
00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.668
(LAUGHS)

196
00:12:39.039 --> 00:12:41.110
Alright. How about I get us another?

197
00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:43.279
It's alright. Play on, play on.

198
00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.716
Now, what are you having, boy?

199
00:12:45.799 --> 00:12:48.315
Oh, Treble rum, please, Reenie.

200
00:12:49.679 --> 00:12:51.318
What about you, Carrots?

201
00:12:51.399 --> 00:12:52.799
I'll have two jars of ale.

202
00:12:52.879 --> 00:12:54.836
Tepid or warm?

203
00:12:55.759 --> 00:12:59.720
Reenie, if you was 50 years younger,
I would dive straight up you.

204
00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:03.510
You dizzy queen, I'm 49.

205
00:13:04.039 --> 00:13:06.157
Life ain't been too kind,
has it, Treacle, hey?

206
00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.038
LESLIE: You will find out soon enough.

207
00:13:09.519 --> 00:13:13.035
Me and Reenie was pulling
babies out the rubble in the Blitz.

208
00:13:13.919 --> 00:13:16.754
Why do you think I'm still here every day?

209
00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:21.991
Cos every day is a gift,
that's why they call it the present.

210
00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.395
(GROANS SOFTLY)

211
00:13:28.919 --> 00:13:29.956
You alright?

212
00:13:32.919 --> 00:13:33.956
Guv'nor.

213
00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:37.755
Your dad is dead!

214
00:13:38.879 --> 00:13:40.599
I said I'm the fucking guv'nor!

215
00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.951
LESLIE:
He's a right raving nutcase, that Roy, sure.

216
00:13:46.039 --> 00:13:48.191
Yeah, well, I am a more raving nutcase.

217
00:13:48.279 --> 00:13:49.918
LESLIE: Oh, let it go, lad.

218
00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.754
He's been committed, you ain't.

219
00:13:53.159 --> 00:13:54.196
Not yet.

220
00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:57.554
REENIE: Roy Shaw did a chunk in Broadmoor.

221
00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.274
Nutted himself out of a cell.

222
00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.716
They said he was blind drunk on Largactil.

223
00:14:01.799 --> 00:14:03.279
They tampered with him.

224
00:14:03.559 --> 00:14:07.110
They gave him electroshock treatment
to control his temper.

225
00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.157
Then they said his ears was burning,

226
00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.677
so they pumped him full of Bavarian ginseng.

227
00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.913
Even the Krays gave him a right wide berth

228
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.309
when they ghosted him out to Parkhurst.

229
00:14:18.399 --> 00:14:21.393
He robs banks and breaks bricks with his nut.

230
00:14:21.519 --> 00:14:23.830
I seen him do it live at the Monday Club.

231
00:14:24.159 --> 00:14:26.038
He's insane.

232
00:14:26.159 --> 00:14:28.197
And he speaks in tongues.

233
00:14:28.279 --> 00:14:31.114
Right. Well, I know what I'm
going to do then.

234
00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:34.671
I'm gonna knock him spark out
and be back in here for lunch.

235
00:14:38.159 --> 00:14:39.798
- Carrots!
- There's a boy.

236
00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:40.915
Ding, ding.

237
00:14:47.159 --> 00:14:48.196
Where is he, then?

238
00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:53.875
Good luck, Lenny.

239
00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:55.755
What?

240
00:14:56.759 --> 00:14:58.513
I'll give you a score. He will need it.

241
00:14:59.519 --> 00:15:00.919
- You alright, son?
- Yeah, I'm alright, mum.

242
00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.317
Ding, ding.

243
00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:08.629
This is Frank Warren, he's promoting you.

244
00:15:09.279 --> 00:15:10.759
He is going places.

245
00:15:10.879 --> 00:15:13.998
- This is Valerie, Carrots.
- Hello sweetheart, Nice to meet you.

246
00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:15.840
And this is our boy, Lenny.

247
